BT 1 0 0 1 0 42.8 Tm 13 TL /F1 9.2 Tf .2 .254902 .333333 rg (At startup GPIO 18 stays low, the high-active relay remains off, ) Tj /F3 9.2 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (COM) Tj /F1 9.2 Tf .2 .254902 .333333 rg ( remains disconnected from ) Tj /F3 9.2 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (NO) Tj /F1 9.2 Tf .2 .254902 .333333 rg (, and the solenoid stays) Tj T* (de-energized. An accepted command drives GPIO 18/) Tj /F3 9.2 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (IN1) Tj /F1 9.2 Tf .2 .254902 .333333 rg ( high, closes ) Tj /F3 9.2 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (COM) Tj /F1 9.2 Tf .2 .254902 .333333 rg ( to ) Tj /F3 9.2 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (NO) Tj /F1 9.2 Tf .2 .254902 .333333 rg (, energizes the solenoid, changes the) Tj T* (indicator to green, sounds the piezo, and drives GPIO 18 low again after five seconds. The firmware also switches the relay) Tj T* (off if Wi-Fi or MQTT connectivity is lost.) Tj T* ET
